      "date": "2026-07-27 22:07:01.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 3:\n\n(5 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. Two of the ported checks no longer reproduce the result of the autoconf test they replace, because the grep pattern matches only the wording the header had in a later kernel than the one that introduced the API. It would be worth running gen_compat.py against the oldest supported kernel for each macro (RHEL8 4.18, RHEL9/SLES15 SP5 5.14, Ubuntu 22.04 5.15, SLES15 SP6/SP7 6.4, RHEL10 6.12) and diffing the result against the config.h produced before the conversion, so the whole batch is confirmed equivalent rather than checked by inspection.",
